# Production UI Standard

Harness Studio is intended for external SaaS users. Every user-visible change must use polished product copy and interaction design suitable for non-technical customers.

- Describe user intent and outcome, not implementation details. Never expose test prompts such as `hello`, IPC or RPC method names, Electron errors, internal service names, stack traces, or transport terminology.
- Convert internal failures into concise actionable Chinese messages. Keep detailed diagnostics in the main-process log only.
- Use stable status language such as “正在检测连接”“连接正常”“连接失败”，and avoid developer-oriented narration.
- Truncate secondary details gracefully, preserve clear visual hierarchy, and verify loading, success, empty, disabled, and failure states before considering UI work complete.
- Treat screenshots and copy as release-quality product surfaces, not development placeholders.
